From: NanoKVM contributors
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: describe SG2002 XTheadVector

The main C906 on SG2002 implements XTheadVector with 128-bit registers.
Describe this in the SoC DTS rather than a carrier overlay. Do not add
the ratified V extension or change the shared CV180x CPU description.

Verified on LicheeRV Nano: VLENB=16, vector byte load/add/store results,
and userspace context switching with the kernel vector support enabled.

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002.dtsi
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002.dtsi
@@ -55,6 +55,13 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&cpu0 {
+	/* The main C906 implements draft 0.7.1, not ratified RVV 1.0. */
+	riscv,isa-extensions = "i", "m", "a", "f", "d", "c", "zicntr", "zicsr",
+			       "zifencei", "zihpm", "xtheadvector";
+	thead,vlenb = <16>;
+};
+
 &sdhci0 {
 	compatible = "sophgo,sg2002-dwcmshc";
 };
